{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution","id":940620,"title":"Diluted themes or natural evolution?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-31T07:58:29-07:00","id":940620,"title":"Diluted themes or natural evolution?","content":"I let myself go off on a tangent in another thread and thought it might be better to move it here. So...<br /> <br /> In your opinion, fellow WtA player, do you feel like the themes in Werewolf have diluted or changed over the course of 1st, 2nd, Rev and W20? If so, how so? And what do you like and dislike about it?<br /> <br /> For example, comparing fluff in Revised and W20, it seems like tribalism and infighting has been immensely reduced. Back in 1st and 2nd, being a Metis was practically a death sentence. Elders throated young garou on a whim, beat down cliaths bold enough to carry a fetish and took them for themselves, spat on BoneGnawers and treated them as less than human, let alone Garou. There had better be a world-shaking event involved if you dared visit another tribe's Sept. And if it wasn't a Corax, you can assume that Fera is about as friendly as a BSD.<br /> <br /> Now... Not everyone played that way (nor is there anything wrong with that. Golden rule and all. If you and your troupe wanted to play Strong-Like-Thunder and enjoyed yourselves, that's awesome), but that's generally how the fluff was written. <br /> <br /> Fast forward a few editions and there's suddenly a lot more teamwork, hope and cooperation. Tribes pack together practically at random (and everyone somehow has something nice to say about the Gnawers), mixed septs are commonplace, the stigma of Weaver tech is rarely mentioned, etc etc etc. Things that were perhaps common differences between Players and NPCs seem to have become much more universal among Garou and Fera.<br /> <br /> So, is it a natural evolution of the game and writing? Selling out to popular trends among players? Or have themes just become lost (or purposefully watered down to dilute the campiness) over the years? What's your take?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12162,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","user":"Crusher-of-Cities","date":". 07-31-2016, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T08:39:23-07:00","id":940630,"title":"","content":"Well, first off, WtA is one of those games where everyone took a different view from the fluff and it evolved in their minds. I've been amazed how some players assumed garou return to birthshape upon sleep or that cubs are trained for a day and then sent to their Rite of Passage. So your experiences, even if based on the fluff, might not match what the writers of future books experienced.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't think any of those things you listed are actually gone, the setting just has evolved over the years. Like I said above, everyone had their own experiences and those affected what they wrote into future books. There are also things like actually trying to match the tribes with their homeland's culture rather than the 1st ed stereotype, for example with the Fenrir losing their racism in revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T09:19:55-07:00","id":940647,"title":"","content":"I always got the impression that being a Metis wasn't as big of a deal by Revised due to the tribe books. Most of the tribe books had this whole &quot;punish and blame the parents and not the metis&quot; view when you read either the tribe's take on the litany, or their view on the metis breed. When I read the revised tribe books it came off to my gaming club that really only the Fianna, and Silver Fangs were terrible to their metis, with Red Talons coming next then the bulk of the tribes having the blame the parents view. Was my gaming group the only one's to get this feel from how things were worded in all those other tribe books? I mean yea we expected a more tolerant view from the CoG and the Gnawers, but the other tribes it felt like a bit of a cop out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T10:31:16-07:00","id":940685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940647#post940647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always got the impression that being a Metis wasn't as big of a deal by Revised due to the tribe books. Most of the tribe books had this whole &quot;punish and blame the parents and not the metis&quot; view when you read either the tribe's take on the litany, or their view on the metis breed. When I read the revised tribe books it came off to my gaming club that really only the Fianna, and Silver Fangs were terrible to their metis, with Red Talons coming next then the bulk of the tribes having the blame the parents view. Was my gaming group the only one's to get this feel from how things were worded in all those other tribe books? I mean yea we expected a more tolerant view from the CoG and the Gnawers, but the other tribes it felt like a bit of a cop out.</div> </div> </div> </div>One factor might be that the writers considered how much a player was actually willing to take and what it actually meant. I mean, if I am honest, the base concept of metis is the igor or the madwoman in the attic. The deformed outcast who still hangs around the edges of the village, doing shit jobs. However, that turned out not to be the narrative for metis that was the best. Instead, the narrative of a disabled person is much more common in revised and even in some 2nd ed books.<br /> <br /> One thing to note about the acceptance is that it is tolerance. The metis will still face violence, beatings, various mental abuses and so on as a child. And there is always a sword of damocles hanging over them if they make mistakes, they might just be killed. In tribes like Shadow Lords and Fenrir, if the metis is useful, why waste it's potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T10:55:43-07:00","id":940697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940685#post940685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One factor might be that the writers considered how much a player was actually willing to take and what it actually meant. I mean, if I am honest, the base concept of metis is the igor or the madwoman in the attic. The deformed outcast who still hangs around the edges of the village, doing shit jobs. However, that turned out not to be the narrative for metis that was the best. Instead, the narrative of a disabled person is much more common in revised and even in some 2nd ed books.<br /> <br /> One thing to note about the acceptance is that it is tolerance. The metis will still face violence, beatings, various mental abuses and so on as a child. And there is always a sword of damocles hanging over them if they make mistakes, they might just be killed. In tribes like Shadow Lords and Fenrir, if the metis is useful, why waste it's potential.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sadly my group never played up your last part with beatings and people looking for them to mess up. I always got &quot;well if you read the revised Shadow Lord book...&quot; treatment. It always bugged me. I also never really got why the Fianna were one of the few who were written to be terrible to their metis, due to being so lock step with the Celts on body purity when they included the legand of Bres into the tribe's back story. In theory that should have been a wake up moment and break the tribe from that tradition.<br /> <br /> By revised I just was never into the breed (the name alone made me feel rather awkward anyway...), because in my gaming circles everyone was all friendly with the metis and there was no social problem for them, just the parents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T11:13:29-07:00","id":940706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940697#post940697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sadly my group never played up your last part with beatings and people looking for them to mess up. I always got &quot;well if you read the revised Shadow Lord book...&quot; treatment. It always bugged me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, all Shadow Lords are induviduals in the end. Just like how various people can have differing opinions on those disabled, so can the garou have of metis. Especially western younger ones who are more used to being allowing. Others might do it subtly, by putting the metis' deformity constantly on the spot and a reason why the metis shouldn't do certain duties.<br /> <br /> What I've done to combat this, is do my own legwork to portray the abuse and mental conditioning a metis goes through. Show how much it has done damage and how the metis is unsure how to treat allowing septmates. Some metis might even reject the kindness for being too 'soft' on them. Some metis might actually crash and burn from the high of not being hated. And others will think the kkind words are lies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940697#post940697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also never really got why the Fianna were one of the few who were written to be terrible to their metis, due to being so lock step with the Celts on body purity when they included the legand of Bres into the tribe's back story. In theory that should have been a wake up moment and break the tribe from that tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's where the weakness of having non-natives write about cultural myths and other stuff shows. They might have thought that was fitting, not realising the context and point of the story.<br /> Just out of curiosity, how would the story have changed Fianna minds, had it been treated as it should have?<br /> <br /> As for the name, yes, I wish they would change it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T11:39:48-07:00","id":940724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940706#post940706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's where the weakness of having non-natives write about cultural myths and other stuff shows. They might have thought that was fitting, not realising the context and point of the story.<br /> Just out of curiosity, how would the story have changed Fianna minds, had it been treated as it should have?</div> </div> </div> </div>This could just be my opinion, but it was early in the Fianna culture. Basically their big hero Nuada (based on the Celtic God) lost an arm fighting against the Fomori defending Tara. Due to the old Celtic custom of perfect body, mind and soul (a tradition the Fianna still have today) he was no longer able to be the high king, and he was replaced by Bres the Beautiful (who was descended from both Duatha De Danann and Fomori in Celtic myth, and had Fomor ties but was Fianna in WtA) to be the new High King because physically he was flawless. He goes on to betray everyone over to the Fomori, and in White Wolf this was almost the end of the Fianna. Nuada gets a silver prosthetic arm and dies defending the Fianna and Tuatha De Danann. So really this to me should have been a big moment for the Fianna to have dropped this whole &quot;perfect body&quot; garbage back in the early iron age (maybe Bronze? I don't have my tribe book on me to fact check). After all a major moment in the tribe was based around canning someone very capable for losing an arm, and replacing them with someone beautiful who then was of the wyrm. Its one of those moments where the tribes follow too closely to an assigned ethnic group (and an outdated one) instead of growing and differentiating from them (for crying out loud in Fianna culture you gain a bad enough of a battle scar, you lose any formal position you hold in the Sept...its picking human culture over Garou culture which always bugged me).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T11:39:56-07:00","id":940725,"title":"","content":"The change was probably caused by an evolution of society's perspectives on disabled people. I generally think that Metis should be uncommon, around 4% of the Garou population, with them doing most of the grunt work of supervising the Kinfolk who take care of the Bawns and the Caerns. Metis are incapable of breeding because of their sterility, so I also think that they tend to serve Garou society by being a safe...outlet for Garou sexuality for Garou who do not want to be bothered with worrying about having children right now with Kinfolk. I also portray them as, paradoxically, being the closest Garou to the Kinfolk, as they are generally more compassionate because they understand being considered to be minor contributors to Garou society, and are often found monitoring wolf packs and human families that contain Kinfolk. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T11:44:41-07:00","id":940726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940725#post940725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so I also think that they tend to serve Garou society by being a safe...outlet for Garou sexuality for Garou who do not want to be bothered with worrying about having children right now with Kinfolk. I also portray them as, paradoxically, being the closest Garou to the Kinfolk, as they are generally more compassionate because they understand being considered to be minor contributors to Garou society, and are often found monitoring wolf packs and human families that contain Kinfolk. .</div> </div> </div> </div>This was actually used by COG revised, in a twisted way. Personally, I do think that that happens, people are people after all. But officially Litany forbids it, since garou cannot mate with garou. Even if they are sterile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T11:47:48-07:00","id":940729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940726#post940726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was actually used by COG revised</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yea things the CoG and Spirals share.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 07-31-2016, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T11:56:56-07:00","id":940734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940729#post940729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yea things the CoG and Spirals share.....</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is why I said it was twisted. Because it is, very twisted and awful way to treat a metis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:57:39-07:00","id":940771,"title":"","content":"If the Metis consents, who are we to judge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T13:08:15-07:00","id":940781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940771#post940771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Metis consents, who are we to judge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that the non-metis typically has power over the metis, and one willing to break the litany for a quick fuck is not going to be very moral, plenty to judge. The non-metis can basically blackmail the metis into consenting, because who is going to listen to a metis about that? Especially given what a metis' thrall is.<br /> <br /> As for the Child of Gaia rite, its use of metis is basically as replacements for other garou. So the metis isn't there because they are the first choice, but because they are sterile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T13:20:36-07:00","id":940800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940726#post940726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was actually used by COG revised, in a twisted way. Personally, I do think that that happens, people are people after all. But officially Litany forbids it, since garou cannot mate with garou. Even if they are sterile.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it involves the Rite of Clouds and Rain, I'd treat it as being very suspect when it comes to canon inclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T13:21:50-07:00","id":940802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940800#post940800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it involves the Rite of Clouds and Rain, I'd treat it as being very suspect when it comes to canon inclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What do you mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T13:24:22-07:00","id":940803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940802#post940802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What do you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>CoG Revised doesn't exist to a lot of us because of that rite. It's such a flagrant breach of customs that its existence is baffling. It's also the only place where I recall metis being sought out as partners is mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T13:34:57-07:00","id":940812,"title":"","content":"Losing a point of temporary Honor to control frenzy for a story is a fair price. It says that the participants have to have demonstrated genuine affection for each other, so it is not actually that abusive, though it is a bit on the...odd side. I do not see what is that wrong with it, since everyone involved understands that it is a secret ritual that is a violation of the Litany (heck, so are Metis, but they exist).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T13:37:44-07:00","id":940815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940812#post940812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Losing a point of temporary Honor to control frenzy for a story is a fair price. It says that the participants have to have demonstrated genuine affection for each other, so it is not actually that abusive, though it is a bit on the...odd side. I do not see what is that wrong with it, since everyone involved understands that it is a secret ritual that is a violation of the Litany (heck, so are Metis, but they exist).</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Because normally, it's a straight out gushing of Renown. What spirits did they get to approve of this? Because rites don't work without a go-ahead from spirits. Also, there's no mechanical benefit described for the rite, which makes it even more suspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T13:56:14-07:00","id":940833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940815#post940815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? Because normally, it's a straight out gushing of Renown. What spirits did they get to approve of this? Because rites don't work without a go-ahead from spirits. Also, there's no mechanical benefit described for the rite, which makes it even more suspect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yea, I just reread the rite, it does only say &quot;everyone involved in the rite loses a temporary point of honor&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T15:25:27-07:00","id":940876,"title":"","content":"Honestly, as a disabled type person myself, one of my house retcons I have waiting for the new edition is that after the perfect metis was born, the metis that were born during and after the 90s weren't sterile, and a group of them have formed their own tribe that only accepts members that are either metis or born to metis parents. They're developing a stable of kinfolk among the neurodiversity and disability communities and earned the grudging respect of the other tribes when they dealt a major blow to the wyrm when they managed to get evidence that O'Tolley's was using fake &quot;clean&quot; slaughterhouses to trick the public while the oreal ones were places of horror into the hands of none other than Temple motherfucking Grandin right before she was set to be part of a Nightly show panel. The result was not only that O'tolleys got smacked with a bunch of lawsuits, but also that Pentax has become a household name known for shady business (thanks to the shows of the various daily show alumni focusing so much on them), though most people still don't know about the spiritual corruption.<br /> <br /> Said as yet unnamed tribe is part of the Concordat of Stars, partly because they understand the potential of human tech to mitigate disability and partly because is no fucking way a tribe of disability rights focused metis would ever be part of the same faction as the Fianna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T16:23:21-07:00","id":940909,"title":"","content":"To put things simple in 1e nothing you could do mattered. In W20 the prophecy of the Pheonix is right there in the openning. Is it a dilusion of the theme or progression of the story is in the eye of the beholder. If Werewolf was to you about going nobly into the dying of the night.. well that's been downplayed. The Garou nation doesn't have to be dysfunctional. The scars of the wars of Rage can be overcome. This doesn't have to be the end.<br /> <br /> On the other hand just because success is possible doesn't mean its GOING to happen. The odds are still stacked in the favor of the wyrm. Garou are still likely to fragment at the worst times, to turn on their Fera(or vice versa) still Hope exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T16:28:12-07:00","id":940915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940909#post940909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand just because success is possible doesn't mean its GOING to happen. The odds are still stacked in the favor of the wyrm. Garou are still likely to fragment at the worst times, to turn on their Fera(or vice versa) still Hope exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this a lot. Sure things look like they are getting better, and I feel that's more along the lines of natural evolution, but if you want to have that fatalist game, it could still be too little too late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T16:36:07-07:00","id":940920,"title":"","content":"The irony is that the real world is worse off in 2016 than it was in 1996. We are closer to nuclear war with China and Russia than we have been in 25 years, we have a maniac in North Korea with multiple nuclear toys, and we have over a billion more people to feed and house. The Middle East and North Africa are slowly dissolving and South America is entering into the worst depression in 80 years. Europe is turning to fascism and xenophopia. While the US is more progressive, which is nice, I do not think we are in an overall better place globally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T16:59:17-07:00","id":940936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940909#post940909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To put things simple in 1e nothing you could do mattered. In W20 the prophecy of the Pheonix is right there in the openning. Is it a dilusion of the theme or progression of the story is in the eye of the beholder. If Werewolf was to you about going nobly into the dying of the night.. well that's been downplayed. The Garou nation doesn't have to be dysfunctional.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who got my start with the game way-back-when, I've always considered exactly this to be the defining theme of Werewolf. The potential for victory was there, but without question all would end in failure because everyone around you is so frustratingly selfish and narrow-sighted. It's a game about going down fighting, or grasping desperately and the last glimmers of hope.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940920#post940920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The irony is that the real world is worse off in 2016 than it was in 1996... I do not think we are in an overall better place globally.</div> </div> </div> </div>That raises some good questions... How would history have gone differently in the WoD? Would supernaturally corrupt politicians push through legislation that makes the Patriot Act blush? Would Pentex-owned Herculean Firearms take advantage of xenophobia and security fears to lobby for automatic weapons in every American household? And what big players would have their strings in the middle East, or what supernatural battlefield would the current strife be a cover for? I'm posting by phone right now, but in only now dawns on me that I never checked any of my 20th books for commentary on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12162,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","user":"Crusher-of-Cities","date":".  Combined posts 07-31-2016, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T17:00:28-07:00","id":940937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940909#post940909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To put things simple in 1e nothing you could do mattered. In W20 the prophecy of the Pheonix is right there in the openning. Is it a dilusion of the theme or progression of the story is in the eye of the beholder. If Werewolf was to you about going nobly into the dying of the night.. well that's been downplayed. The Garou nation doesn't have to be dysfunctional. The scars of the wars of Rage can be overcome. This doesn't have to be the end.<br /> <br /> On the other hand just because success is possible doesn't mean its GOING to happen. The odds are still stacked in the favor of the wyrm. Garou are still likely to fragment at the worst times, to turn on their Fera(or vice versa) still Hope exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding to this, as stated before, the world and our views have changed. In a lot of ways, we live in the world WoD had in the 80s-90s. In others, so much progress has been made. Plus, when WtA was first created, it was a sort of gothic gaia's revenge against civilization that was still poorly defined and most of its tribes were stereotypes. And honestly, it fit the time, that is why I am not bothered by it existing.<br /> <br /> But it needed to evolve, rather than stay the same. The tribes needed to be cleaned up and considered more, the world was not really as black and white as it seemed. I think the books actually starting to portray Weaver things in a grayer light is sign of the setting maturing into understanding that the fight against the Wyrm is not a simple one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T17:04:34-07:00","id":940940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940936#post940936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That raises some good questions... How would history have gone differently in the WoD? Would supernaturally corrupt politicians push through legislation that makes the Patriot Act blush? Would Pentex-owned Herculean Firearms take advantage of xenophobia and security fears to lobby for automatic weapons in every American household? And what big players would have their strings in the middle East, or what supernatural battlefield would the current strife be a cover for? I'm posting by phone right now, but in only now dawns on me that I never checked any of my 20th books for commentary on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, do we really -need- to portray the situation worse than it all ready is?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T17:07:19-07:00","id":940942,"title":"","content":"...so....anyone want to touch and WoD out the current American Presidential election?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T17:21:45-07:00","id":940952,"title":"","content":"Well, it is a conflict between the Camarilla (Clinton) and the Sabbat (Trump). The Sabbat is losing and is using one of its revenants, who was flesh crafted to look like Trump in 2000, on a long term plan to gain the presidency so that they can turn the US government against the Camarilla. His lack of human experience, however, is showing in the inane and conflicting things that he is saying. His Sabbat handlers do not understand humanity, so they do not understand how badly his statements can backfire. Oh, Russia is under Sabbat control and Putin is also a fleshcrafted revenant that replaced him in 2000.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T17:30:29-07:00","id":940956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940920#post940920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The irony is that the real world is worse off in 2016 than it was in 1996. We are closer to nuclear war with China and Russia than we have been in 25 years,</div> </div> </div> </div>No we aren't. China is too dependent on us as consumers for a nuclear war. Now an ocean based war over the South china sea. Even less so chance with Russia.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> we have a maniac in North Korea with multiple nuclear toys, </div> </div> </div>North Korea had Weapons grade Plutonium in 1996. They've just acknowledged ti to the rest of the world more recently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and we have over a billion more people to feed and house. </div> </div> </div>Population growth has steadily slowed down.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Middle East and North Africa are slowly dissolving and South America is entering into the worst depression in 80 years. Europe is turning to fascism and xenophopia. While the US is more progressive, which is nice, I do not think we are in an overall better place globally. </div> </div> </div><br /> Not that any of this would matter to Garou. Enviromentally the climate Change is a thing. Most of the world acknowledges and even china is willing to do something about.. America is lagging behind on that. But we will see with this election.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T17:36:03-07:00","id":940958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940942#post940942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...so....anyone want to touch and WoD out the current American Presidential election?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not since the Second World war has the Nephandi made such a blatant play on an international level. Nihilism and destruction are the vote to be cast. Vengence, Xenophobia.. the Technocracy has lost the Tiger.. fortunately they have an operative on the other side.. Maybe they need to let in certain &quot;tradition&quot; elements under a banner of unity... but the Sleepers must be protected and better superstionalists who want a better world than ones who want to see it burn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T17:48:54-07:00","id":940964,"title":"","content":"China is doing nothing for the environment. It is the largest producer of carbon dioxide emissions and they are still building new coal fired power plants. The US emissions have been going down for the last ten years, due to the transition from coal to natural gas, and are 500 million metric tons less in 2015 than 2005. Compare that to China, which is 10 billion metric tons more in 2015 than 2005, and you will see that the US is doing much more than China for saving the environment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member