er":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T10:20:27-07:00","id":942048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=941826#post941826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">World of Sunshine. Why isn't that a game?<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>What is wrong with a little success in that department? Means at least the animal kinfolk have gotten a break.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T09:35:48-07:00","id":942763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=941998#post941998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No lone Khan with all the game in the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>well that too of course. But the Chinese mafia are the biggest tiger poachers around. I could see the Khans somehow doing to the tiger penis bones what the game wardens in south africa have been doing to Rhino horns. If you don't know what I am talking about, Rhino Rescue folks have been injecting Rhino horns with a poison that is harmless to the Rhinos but makes humans (such as Chinese folks that use the horns for medicine) very sick. I bet there is a gift that could do the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T12:11:40-07:00","id":942894,"title":"","content":"What about the USA? There are as many as 10,000 captive tigers in the USA, so I imagine that the Khan are concerned about the treatment of their animal Kinfolk in the US as much as they are about their animal Kinfolk in Chinese tiger farms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T12:52:09-07:00","id":942931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=942894#post942894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the USA? There are as many as 10,000 captive tigers in the USA, so I imagine that the Khan are concerned about the treatment of their animal Kinfolk in the US as much as they are about their animal Kinfolk in Chinese tiger farms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, because keeping some tigers as pets is the same as driving them to extinction because of their magic dicks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T13:48:21-07:00","id":942968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=942894#post942894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the USA? There are as many as 10,000 captive tigers in the USA, so I imagine that the Khan are concerned about the treatment of their animal Kinfolk in the US as much as they are about their animal Kinfolk in Chinese tiger farms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I used to be a zoo keeper, and we researched this stuff a lot. Unfortunately if that number counts privately held tigers, a lot of them do not really conform to any subspecies of tigers, but instead of a mingling of the different subspecies. We raised our big cats (and honestly the goal was all of our animals) to act as close to the wild counterparts as possible. We would explain to visitors the goal was to have a tiger that hopefully some day maybe could be released (though through a long process, not just our zoo to the wild), and not a bunch of huge orange generic felines. I wonder what a &quot;spiritual&quot; toll captivity and especially in the case of tigers people want to do magic with/take photos with/and breed with any ol'tiger instead of maintain certain lineages could be.....after all, CB20 states that while there are wild pigs still, all the Grondr kin are all dead.<br /> <br /> Then again, maybe I'm just really biased against &quot;ZMOG AWESOME I WANT A PET TIGER!!!!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 08-03-2016, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:18:47-07:00","id":943811,"title":"","content":"My god. I wanted to kill a player one time so much, but we were playing a one-on-one session, so I just gave him a stern warning.<br /> <br /> His claith Die-ultimae glass walker had just escaped with a black fury from a former hive used by skin-dancers.<br /> They approached an unknown sept in the umbra.<br /> They gave howls. The howl back was a Wendigo saying 'Yeah,Nah bro, This is wendigo territory, We don't want glass walkers here.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now the player, Idiot as he is, ignored this warning and went towards the moon bridge.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should have killed him there.<br /> <br /> The Impressive Crinos who gave the howl and who guarded the bridge, was understandably mad.<br /> The player, and the glass walker, being a pair of idiots, backtalked the guy.<br /> <br /> Probably should have killed him there<br /> <br /> The wendigo, Being as diplomatic as an ahroun wendigo experiencing sass from a young glass walker could be, Told the glass walker to leave<br /> The glass walker, being a fucking idiot, Tried to leave via the septs moon bridge<br /> <br /> Should have killed him there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I get that the player was playing a problematic ragabash, but... <b>The kids just don't fucking get garou society at all.<br /> Garou are supposed to be dickheads</b>. The war would have been won and the Apocalypse a distant non-threat if they could all just get <i>along</i>.<br /> And I think they don't get that, and I don't think the writters get that. <b>The world of darkness is just getting too light.</b> Stuff like the Ahadi is just.... A joke. If everyone gets along then there's no conflict. And if there's no conflict... what's the point of playing world of darkness. You're literally a bunch of brainwashed, anger fueled psychopaths who think they're a benevolent God's gift to the world. There's no room to be social or liberal. You belong in a pecking order and you're a part of tribes (each with it's own crippling social weakness, might i add). I don't care if you have five intelligence and ten willpower, The Intelligence is used to justify your bullshit, and the willpower is there to make you stubborn (or if it's lacking: Suggestible) and in the event you were adopted into the tribe unknowing of your garou heritage, you might have the capability to resist the ideas of those galliards with consistent 4's across their social stats. You're a crusader in the modern age and everyone but the spider-tainted thinks the best weapon ever is an oversized silver knife in an age of fully automatic rifles.<br /> <br /> The garou are supposed to be loosing because the garou nation is fucked. Meanwhile the fera will still try to avenge themselves for one of the wars of rage and the spirits all think they're right about stuff because most of them are one-concept guys. If you look across the splat for Changing breed powers and wonderous fetishes, you think to yourself 'how can they be loosing when they have stuff like this?' and the answer is simple: The Changers cause almost as many problems as they fix.<br /> <br /> And I don't think a lot of people <i>get</i> this. We're not exactly going for 40k grimdark, but I think w20 (and to some extent v20 and also m20 is in a lot of ways a progressive joke) doesn't really highlight this as much as it needs to be said. World of darkness just isn't that dark anymore, and I think that undermines it terribly. Heck in M20 half the traditions get name changes to make them more 'pc'. A fucking <i>joke</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:27:16-07:00","id":943818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=940920#post940920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The irony is that the real world is worse off in 2016 than it was in 1996. We are closer to nuclear war with China and Russia than we have been in 25 years, we have a maniac in North Korea with multiple nuclear toys...</div> </div> </div> </div>And infinitely better than at any time prior to that. There is no Soviet Union, and Russia is having issues holding on to its ill-gotten gains in Ukraine -- taking on NATO is probably not in the cards. As for North Korea, they probably don't have the ability to put any of their nukes on a missile, half of which simply blow up on the pad, and none of which have the ability to hit the U.S. mainland. Also, they know exactly what will happen to them if they were to try against South Korea or Japan. MAD still works just fine as a concept, even after 70 years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...so....anyone want to touch and WoD out the current American Presidential election?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wanted to add that Trump is hinted as being a member of the Star Chamber in Project Twilight.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:41:26-07:00","id":943834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=943811#post943811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I don't think a lot of people <i>get</i> this. We're not exactly going for 40k grimdark, but I think w20 (and to some extent v20 and also m20 is in a lot of ways a progressive joke) doesn't really highlight this as much as it needs to be said. World of darkness just isn't that dark anymore, and I think that undermines it terribly. Heck in M20 half the traditions get name changes to make them more 'pc'. A fucking <i>joke</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a question, why does your dark gothic RPG need to have stereotyped or just utterly false representations of other races/nationalities? What in those helps the mood of the session? What do they actually -add- to the game?<br /> <br /> Because, here's a thing, people from all over the world play WoD. People who love the game, but dislike how it gets so much of their culture wrong. These people, as much as any other player, deserve to be treated fairly. And that means that the writers do their research and correct their mistakes.<br /> <br /> I've seen a lot of people claim being pc is the reason WoD or some other media isn't dark anymore. All pc is supposed to be, is that various races/sexualities/etc. are given a proper due. There is a lot of good horror to be gained from actual stories from around the world, and we should listen.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:38:22-07:00","id":943889,"title":"","content":"Personally the creation of things like the Ahadi does not mean that the shifters are 100% on the road to saving the world. You can still play a lot of in fighting and politicing if you decide to play an Ahadi game. Years ago in college my gaming group were playing 2nd edition WtA because we had no clue revised had come out (we were all working off one friend's collection of books). We created an American equivalent of the Ahadi before we knew it existed. We had politicing from within, the Ratkin despised the concept and constantly worked against it, the Fera didn't trust the Garou all that much, and the Garou felt they should have a greater say over the Fera because they were a bigger vote, Latin American, Caribbean, and Canadian shfiters were paranoid of American shifters pulling a First Among Equals move. Even then the Garou tribes didn't agree on the move with the Fangs and Shadow Lords using it as a wedge to gain influence among the other tribes. We had the organization clash with the Beast Courts in places like California where we decided a long history of Asian immigration would have produced an expansion of the courts into newer territory. When characters traveld abroad they got a new fresh dose of paranoia from the locals because they were convinced that the only reason the American shifters would band together was to be stronger as an &quot;American&quot; (as in U.S. and not the continents) and begin to take territory/impose their will on Fera from other parts of the world.<br /> <br /> The same thing can happen in the Ahadi, the Simba can shoot for too much power, or work to destroy it from with in, could use the Ajaba who are bent on vengeance to destroy it (have them still killing Simba then running to the Ahadi and claiming the lions are still unjustly looking for an excuse to hunt them), or the Ahadi could evolve to feel that by virtue of being a shifter in Africa, you ARE in the Ahadi and all of your bases belong to us!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:55:51-07:00","id":943907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=943834#post943834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's a question, why does your dark gothic RPG need to have stereotyped or just utterly false representations of other races/nationalities? What in those helps the mood of the session? What do they actually -add- to the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. That's fine. Actually getting the representation of other cultures/races/nationalities is great. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=943834#post943834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen a lot of people claim being pc is the reason WoD or some other media isn't dark anymore. All pc is supposed to be, is that various races/sexualities/etc. are given a proper due. </div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. When there's one section of magadon pharmacuticals that's leader isn't knowingly influenced by the wyrm but rather feminism, you really start to question what's what with white wolf. When you look at how 'cultural appropriation' is a terrifying weaver spirit out to drive creative thoughts from our head... <br /> While it's nice to have a few updates on getting things correct with Euthanatos thinking about a name change and the Assamites turning into cool bros through the power of retcon, stuff like the Sons of Ether turning into the Society of Ether...<br /> <br /> It's nice and all, but it's undermining the world of darkness. The setting is supposed to be sexist, racist and full of hate, and I suppose it's a setting where a lot more 'liberals' are really just angry conservatives wanting safe spaces and the demise of white males; But in-setting discrimination is perfectly appropriate. Droping 'Brotherhood' From the Akashics and trading sons for Society is not in the same vein of thought as making Assamites and Ravnos not actually the terrible stereotypes that everyone thinks they are. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:59:08-07:00","id":943912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=943907#post943907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. That's fine. Actually getting the representation of other cultures/races/nationalities is great.<br /> [COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]<br /> Droping 'Brotherhood' From the Akashics and trading sons for Society is not in the same vein of thought as making Assamites and Ravnos not actually the terrible stereotypes that everyone thinks they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean about the Assamites and the Ravnos? I have V20 stuff but I'm not sure I read it close enough to catch what you are referencing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T19:40:54-07:00","id":944085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=943811#post943811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The garou are supposed to be loosing because the garou nation is fucked. Meanwhile the fera will still try to avenge themselves for one of the wars of rage and the spirits all think they're right about stuff because most of them are one-concept guys. If you look across the splat for Changing breed powers and wonderous fetishes, you think to yourself 'how can they be loosing when they have stuff like this?' and the answer is simple: The Changers cause almost as many problems as they fix.<br /> <br /> And I don't think a lot of people <i>get</i> this. We're not exactly going for 40k grimdark, but I think w20 (and to some extent v20 and also m20 is in a lot of ways a progressive joke) doesn't really highlight this as much as it needs to be said. World of darkness just isn't that dark anymore, and I think that undermines it terribly. Heck in M20 half the traditions get name changes to make them more 'pc'. A fucking <i>joke</i></div> </div> </div> </div>You're the one not getting it. Its right there in the god damned book. Prophecy of the Phoenix right at the beginning. A setting without Hope is 40k Grimdark. The intention of the new editions is to remove the whole &quot;Screw you Hippie&quot; mindset of making a whole bunch of completely unplayable splats. That's the point of the Ahdi, and the Emerald Courts and Shattered Dream all having ways to play multiple breeds together.<br /> <br /> As for the Traditions Changes Amazingly non European groups might want to.. I don't know use theriown names rather than what the Order of Hermes slapped on them in the 14th century. the Akashayana were what they'd always called themselves, the Sahajiya wanting to be taken more seriously than the Cox(or seers of Chronos) the Kha'vadi wanting to have theirown damned name, the Chakravanti returning to their Origional name from teh Dark ages/Sorcerer's Crusade. I'd sure as hell like to know how the Virtual Adept change to Mercurial Elite is anything but times change. The only thing that is slightly &quot;politically correct&quot; is the Society of Ether but honestly they've change names about once a century. <br /> <br /> Darkness is meaningless without Hope.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T08:45:34-07:00","id":944338,"title":"","content":"I feel like the sense of hope in the metaplot is really a kind of endgame &quot;you're winning&quot; kind of stage, where players have contributed enough over the years to see the light at the end of the tunnel. Having this be the starting point/Default assumption really undermines the core theme of the game, especially werewolf. In world of darkness, you should be earning your salvation. The point of the game is to make the world for you less shit. No point at all if it's already doing that itself, is there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T15:08:40-07:00","id":944550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=944338#post944338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the sense of hope in the metaplot is really a kind of endgame &quot;you're winning&quot; kind of stage, where players have contributed enough over the years to see the light at the end of the tunnel. Having this be the starting point/Default assumption really undermines the core theme of the game, especially werewolf. In world of darkness, you should be earning your salvation. The point of the game is to make the world for you less shit. No point at all if it's already doing that itself, is there?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't. I think a complete and utter lack of hope is exactly 40k Grimdark. &quot;Earning Hope&quot; is 40k Grimdark. The fact that the Ahdi exists didn't suddenly &quot;Win the appocalypse in africa&quot; they wyrm is more powerful than ever. the Wyrm has a whole damn Mockery Breed down there. The Emerald Courts have Existed for Thousands of Years..and China is one of the most poluted countries on the planet.<br /> <br /> Just because &quot;We can all get along&quot; doesn't mean the Fera aren't doomed to fail because they have the wrong tools for the job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T17:18:07-07:00","id":944602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=943907#post943907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. That's fine. Actually getting the representation of other cultures/races/nationalities is great.<br /> [COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]<br /> Eh. When there's one section of magadon pharmacuticals that's leader isn't knowingly influenced by the wyrm but rather feminism,</div> </div> </div> </div>The higher ups in the company keep her on-staff entirely to make it look like they care about women's issues in some way other than potential business ventures. Alas, it is Magadon, and as a corporation, it knows only a desire for glutting itself on profit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> you really start to question what's what with white wolf. When you look at how 'cultural appropriation' is a terrifying weaver spirit out to drive creative thoughts from our head... </div> </div> </div>Werewolf has always abhorred what Cultural Appropriation and its earlier kin represent, since what it does is what's pretty much happening to the Garou and Fera and cultures that they've typically clustered around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While it's nice to have a few updates on getting things correct with Euthanatos thinking about a name change and the Assamites turning into cool bros through the power of retcon, stuff like the Sons of Ether turning into the Society of Ether...<br /> <br /> It's nice and all, but it's undermining the world of darkness. The setting is supposed to be sexist, racist and full of hate,and I suppose it's a setting where a lot more 'liberals' are really just angry conservatives wanting safe spaces and the demise of white males; But in-setting discrimination is perfectly appropriate. Droping 'Brotherhood' From the Akashics and trading sons for Society is not in the same vein of thought as making Assamites and Ravnos not actually the terrible stereotypes that everyone thinks they are. </div> </div> </div>The setting is a horribly unkind place, but it's still a game meant to be played, discussed, and support a pretty wide variety of stories. There is a point where a setting can become so unappealing that people just put the book down and don't play or buy new books in droves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T17:52:59-07:00","id":944620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=944602#post944602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The setting is a horribly unkind place, but it's still a game meant to be played, discussed, and support a pretty wide variety of stories. There is a point where a setting can become so unappealing that people just put the book down and don't play or buy new books in droves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding to this, there is a reason why Warhammer 40k is mainly a miniature game. It is much easier to process deaths of so many, when it is more about strategy than exploring the world through the eyes of one character.<br /> <br /> And even when they do, there are characters like Ciaphas Cain. Guys who might be selfish, but who still try to do the best they can with what they have.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T02:09:02-07:00","id":946027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=942048#post942048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is wrong with a little success in that department? Means at least the animal kinfolk have gotten a break.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing. Well, it doesn't really go well, with the &quot;Word of <b>DARKNESS</b>&quot; feel, that is inherently pessimistic and ... well ... dark. Or is at least meant to be so.<br /> <br /> Media tend to show us all the terrible things that happen in the world more often than the positive ones and I think the &quot;one World of Darkness&quot; that Martin talks about for the future editions of the WoD-games will be equally dreary. Mainly because, as we see in BNS's Werewolf book, the times between the end of the revised edition and the present are filled with a catastrophe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, I'm not sure what the themes and moods in Werewolf 1st Edition were, according to the core rules. But, for me the focus was, much like in Forsaken, with the pack of player characters and their adventures in their territory. I could have the Savage Horror as well as personal elements and some politics with sept NPCs without the need of global metaplots, changes, characters and so on. And I found the focus of the game changed towards such elements and I didn't like that.<br /> I can see, that games where you can influence the whole world with your character have their appeal. But werewolf wasn't that for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T07:27:32-07:00","id":946150,"title":"","content":"I generally prefer the World of Darkness to be the shadow of our world rather than a twisted reflection. Our world is unspeakably cruel and billions suffer from grinding poverty and exploitation. To make our world the world of darkness, you just have to remove the filters that you use to maintain your sanity and allow yourself to see the truth. The supernatural creatures are just an added spice that makes playing in the world of darkness interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T13:33:35-07:00","id":946414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=946150#post946150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally prefer the World of Darkness to be the shadow of our world rather than a twisted reflection. Our world is unspeakably cruel and billions suffer from grinding poverty and exploitation. To make our world the world of darkness, you just have to remove the filters that you use to maintain your sanity and allow yourself to see the truth. The supernatural creatures are just an added spice that makes playing in the world of darkness interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This. I very much feel the &quot;Our world but darker&quot; comes from a level of unexamined privlege that's not worth keeping.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for being on topic. The world is worse enviromentally, and no more closer to magic being treated as real so to me any revision in werewolf or mage is much closer to moving deck chairs around on the titanic than &quot;HEY WE ARE WINNING&quot;. Those are the win conditions for those games not &quot;Fera get back to the point they were 10,000 years ago&quot; or &quot;Nonwestern Mages get to use theirown words!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:18:59-07:00","id":946452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=946150#post946150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally prefer the World of Darkness to be the shadow of our world rather than a twisted reflection. Our world is unspeakably cruel and billions suffer from grinding poverty and exploitation. To make our world the world of darkness, you just have to remove the filters that you use to maintain your sanity and allow yourself to see the truth. The supernatural creatures are just an added spice that makes playing in the world of darkness interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to go a step farther, in no small part due to the fact that there are so many forces actively pushing the envelope in the WoD. Sure, we all like to sit around and talk about government corruption, the power of lobbyists, and heartless corporations... but in the WoD there is zero question that people own massive numbers of the police, who actively cover up certain crimes. Herculean Firearms is a powerful lobby that wants machineguns in every toddler's hands in a world where racism and impotent rage is ten times more powerful and far less thinly veiled. There is literal taint in that Double O'Tolley's with Cheese* that makes people more slothful and gluttonous, and drinking enough King's Liquor can literally brainwash you into a chauvenistic, date-raping, wife-beater.<br /> <br /> Reflection of the real world is certainly a good jumping point... but, for example, there's no way the Ebola outbreak in West Africa over the last two years went anywhere near as smoothly in the WoD as it did in our world. Not with the most numerous shifter race on the planet being so obsessed with genocide and conveniently immune to disease.<br /> <br /> *Cheese refers to a cheese-flavored food product. Contains no actual cheese.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T16:36:22-07:00","id":946546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=946452#post946452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend to go a step farther, in no small part due to the fact that there are so many forces actively pushing the envelope in the WoD. Sure, we all like to sit around and talk about government corruption, the power of lobbyists, and heartless corporations... but in the WoD there is zero question that people own massive numbers of the police, who actively cover up certain crimes. Herculean Firearms is a powerful lobby that wants machineguns in every toddler's hands in a world where racism and impotent rage is ten times more powerful and far less thinly veiled. There is literal taint in that Double O'Tolley's with Cheese* that makes people more slothful and gluttonous, and drinking enough King's Liquor can literally brainwash you into a chauvenistic, date-raping, wife-beater.<br /> <br /> Reflection of the real world is certainly a good jumping point... but, for example, there's no way the Ebola outbreak in West Africa over the last two years went anywhere near as smoothly in the WoD as it did in our world. Not with the most numerous shifter race on the planet being so obsessed with genocide and conveniently immune to disease.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except then you go down the road into having to create your own full on alt history. You say the WOD is more racist.. does that mean Obama was never elected? You say there's &quot;no way the ebola oubreak in West Africa&quot; could have been the same because shifters were involved.. so what does that mean we should be running Africa like its the Stand? And why doesn't &quot;The Techncracy/Weaver etc&quot; counter act any Shifter game play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T17:27:53-07:00","id":946563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=946546#post946546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Except then you go down the road into having to create your own full on alt history. You say the WOD is more racist.. does that mean Obama was never elected? You say there's &quot;no way the ebola oubreak in West Africa&quot; could have been the same because shifters were involved.. so what does that mean we should be running Africa like its the Stand? And why doesn't &quot;The Techncracy/Weaver etc&quot; counter act any Shifter game play?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Having to make alt history IS a natural pitfall for that... but generally I go with the law of wibbly-wobbly timey-wimey. Namely, even if the path has changed, the outcome is generally the same. Everything bad is just... more. There are racists who hate Obama in the real world (of course I'm sure there are non-racists that also hate him, but that's not the topic here)... therefore there are MORE in the World of Darkness. Maybe instead of dozens of threats against him, maybe there were a few attempts. In the end, we still get to the same place... but that path was just a lot nastier.<br /> <br /> So the Ebola outbreak is solved or nearly so.... but the disease spread further, claimed more lives, broke quarantine a few times and caused a larger panic. Mass shootings are a little more mass, and a little more frequent. Reactions are a little more knee-jerk and a little more polarized (if such a thing was possible). Gun stores sell out a little faster for a little longer after each one. Automatic weapons are a little easier to get, and the laws are a little looser. The evils and moral failings of the small minorities that the media love to spotlight are found a little further out into the bell-curve, and suddenly there's a little truth to whatever Alex Jones is accusing someone of this week. <br /> <br /> Like most folks, I agree that our own world is plenty dark, but I've always seen the World of Darkness as more of a caricature than a reflection. Every feature and every flaw in our society is exaggerated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T17:48:22-07:00","id":946583,"title":"","content":"I do not think that you need the world of darkness to be any darker than our world. Why are diseases not killing more people? Because increased disease fatalities would reduce the human population, which would reduce the amount of suffering in the world, which would reduce the corruption of the Wyrm. I do not think that the Ahadi are not numerous enough to combat Pentex fomori, African vampires, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T19:59:22-07:00","id":946694,"title":"","content":"Ok so here is a question with the debate about how close should the game mirror our own world...with wererats around who's very job is to curb human population....how do people match that up with the population size of China and India for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T21:17:30-07:00","id":946727,"title":"","content":"Incompetent Ratkin? Pentex designer immunizations against Ratkin plagues? Dharma 5+ Kuei-jin sucking the Chi out of every Ratkin they find through breath stealing because they taste like chicken? All three? Anyway, Ratkin are really rare, there may be only as many Ratkin as there are Garou (14,000 or so globally) and they are kind of squishy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T21:33:47-07:00","id":946735,"title":"","content":"They don't give numbers but they do state that there are more Ratkin then Garou....and when you're handing out infectious diseases you don't really need many because your weapon is legion onto itself, and in that case you don't really need to be putting yourself in situations where &quot;squishy&quot; matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T23:42:41-07:00","id":946770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=946727#post946727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incompetent Ratkin? Pentex designer immunizations against Ratkin plagues? Dharma 5+ Kuei-jin sucking the Chi out of every Ratkin they find through breath stealing because they taste like chicken? All three? Anyway, Ratkin are really rare, there may be only as many Ratkin as there are Garou (14,000 or so globally) and they are kind of squishy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just no. To all of that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=946694#post946694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so here is a question with the debate about how close should the game mirror our own world...with wererats around who's very job is to curb human population....how do people match that up with the population size of China and India for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even with the numbers they have, there aren't enough of them. And in the modern times, they seem to have lost their way quite a bit. At this point, they seem to be gearing up for the Apocalypse to cleanse the world. You could also make the argument that without them, the human population might be even higher than it is now. But mostly, from my point of view, they quit really pursuing their job a long time ago. Now they just kind of curb population as a pastime. They're kind of crazy now in general.<br /> <br /> Come the Apocalypse though, I could see some nests infecting 100% of the kinfolk they can find just for the pure chaos it would bring. Even if only 10% complete the Change, the number of frenzied/raptured Ratkin running around would be horrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T00:09:26-07:00","id":946780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=946694#post946694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so here is a question with the debate about how close should the game mirror our own world...with wererats around who's very job is to curb human population....how do people match that up with the population size of China and India for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ratkin have been &quot;slacking off&quot; practically until the last 30 or so years. Only in that time have they begun their massive breeding projects.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T01:08:31-07:00","id":946803,"title":"","content":"It always bugs me when people just assume that doing Gaia's work is not only easy, but also a no-brainer. Give the rats a break, keeping the global human population down is a tall order!<br /> <br /> Indeed, they have done a pretty decent job managing it up until the last century and a half or so.<br /> I chalk it up to the Ratkin's natural methods of plaguebreeding failing to keep up with modern medicinal advancement. When you consider how long the wererats have been around, why would they expect that afflictions like typhoid, scarlet fever and influenza would stop killing people? Such things were devastating throughout human existence right up until this century; a blink in the eye for shifter civilization!<br /> <br /> Only recently have diseases begun to develop resistances and now the pendulum is swinging the other way...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T05:05:32-07:00","id":946874,"title":"","content":"Sanitation, vaccinations, and antibiotics are just three reasons why diseases are no longer population control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T07:26:16-07:00","id":946924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=946803#post946803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It always bugs me when people just assume that doing Gaia's work is not only easy, but also a no-brainer. Give the rats a break, keeping the global human population down is a tall order!<br /> <br /> Indeed, they have done a pretty decent job managing it up until the last century and a half or so.<br /> I chalk it up to the Ratkin's natural methods of plaguebreeding failing to keep up with modern medicinal advancement. When you consider how long the wererats have been around, why would they expect that afflictions like typhoid, scarlet fever and influenza would stop killing people? Such things were devastating throughout human existence right up until this century; a blink in the eye for shifter civilization!<br /> <br /> Only recently have diseases begun to develop resistances and now the pendulum is swinging the other way...</div> </div> </div> </div>Also the Ratkin as a group don't seem to be working towards half measures currently vs the Stand/Walking Dead scenarios.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T08:37:32-07:00","id":946963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=946803#post946803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It always bugs me when people just assume that doing Gaia's work is not only easy, but also a no-brainer. Give the rats a break, keeping the global human population down is a tall order!</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't going with it was easy, I was intentionally bringing up the two population extremes. In these two regions humans have had a much bigger boost in population then in other parts of the world. I get that they are very recent (especially as far as shifters are concerned), but they are also rather extreme as well. <br /> <br /> So people bring up that the Ratkin have been slacking/are side tracked, would that include the Nezumi then? Since from what I've read they seemed more sane then their counterparts in the rest of the world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:18:08-07:00","id":946989,"title":"","content":"The thing about china is that their high population skews older, to the point where the Chinese economy might melt down in the next few decades due to the cost of caring for all those elderly people. And since economic recessions tend to lower carbon emissions due to all the factories that shut down, that could be good thing for Gaia and what not. I wouldn't be surprised if the smarter rat kin let the Chinese population boom like that for just that reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:41:38-07:00","id":947022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=946963#post946963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't going with it was easy, I was intentionally bringing up the two population extremes. In these two regions humans have had a much bigger boost in population then in other parts of the world. I get that they are very recent (especially as far as shifters are concerned), but they are also rather extreme as well.<br /> <br /> So people bring up that the Ratkin have been slacking/are side tracked, would that include the Nezumi then? Since from what I've read they seemed more sane then their counterparts in the rest of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly we don't know what a &quot;Working as intended&quot; Fera looks like. Especially not a Ratkin. We know that currently the Ratkin are just building up large numbers and planning full on human Genocide. We know in the past they've done a pretty good job of this... see North America.<br /> <br /> We know the Hengeyokai are closer to &quot;working as intended&quot; but even they are missing major chunks of the puzzle(Bears, Aurochs, Bats, Boars). Are the Nezumi failing to live up to their breed role by playing too nice with others? Its possible.. on the other hand there's a very powerful Yama Queen who feeds on disease, which might be what's holding back that tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T11:48:46-07:00","id":947131,"title":"","content":"I think some thing needs to be taken into account in this discussion. Mainly, that WoD books weren't just the text and just the issues of the times. It was also the artwork and the themes brought fort with them.<br /> <br /> Look at any 1st ed tribebook, just look at the art it has and the themes it uses. The opening comics, the templates offered and the way things are presented.<br /> <br /> To me, it often is rather goofy and very cartoony, much more like a comic book than anything else. And that continues to early 2nd ed. But through that edition to Revised and from there to W20, things matured a lot. The art got more detailed and refined, the books got better editing and layouts, and more pages. Research was done much more on the topics, and revised stated outright the alpha-omega thing was a myth, long before that became more well known.<br /> <br /> Also, to use one very specific example, look at how treatment of BDSM and body modification has changed through WoD. In the first, it is used almost solely to be edgy or show wyrm taint. And that continues in 2nd ed artwork. In revised,it's use like that lessened, and by w20 it is pretty much gone. Times changed, but so did the way WtA was.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T12:40:45-07:00","id":947166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/940620-diluted-themes-or-natural-evolution?p=946874#post946874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sanitation, vaccinations, and antibiotics are just three reasons why diseases are no longer population control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Antibiotics are rapidly being outpaced by resistance on account of how much longer it takes to develop drugs than for infectious organisms to develop resistances to them. Many drugs that do get developed are also very expensive, preventing widespread use, which oddly enough, keeps their effectiveness up for a longer period of time. As opposed to the current standard of prophylactic and agricultural use of antibiotics, which is why MRSA and its ilk are a thing.<br /> <br /> Of course, bacteria are also not the only infectious agents out there. If the rats get really desperate, they might start actively spreading prion diseases.<br /> <br /> Sanitation might also take a hit, depending on how well the infrastructure is doing. And if Twitchers plant bombs in said infrastructure, which in the US is actually getting strained and outdated, well, suddenly you have a whole lot of old problems resurfacing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}